IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`
IMPORT `er4-part3-reduction`

-- Tests of regs 60, 61 and 62 (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1012-1036). Every expected value is written by hand from the
-- text, never copied from the module's output. The figures are invented for the tests; none is a published figure.

§ `Reg 60 -- plan`

-- The definition says a plan is a wage-loss plan covering insured persons employed by an employer, and INCLUDES the four named kinds.
#ASSERT `reg 60 plan` `er4 another wage-loss plan` TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 60 plan` `er4 a Weekly Indemnity Plan` FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 60 plan` `er4 an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 60 plan` `er4 another wage-loss plan` FALSE

§ `Reg 61 -- the Part applies where the insured persons benefit from at least 5/12 of the reduction`

#ASSERT `reg 61 five-twelfths of the reduction of the employer's premium` 1200 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `reg 61 five-twelfths of the reduction of the employer's premium` 12 EQUALS 5
-- At exactly five-twelfths ("at least equal to"), above it, and just below it.
#ASSERT `reg 61 this Part applies` TRUE 1200 500
#ASSERT `reg 61 this Part applies` TRUE 1200 501
#ASSERT NOT `reg 61 this Part applies` TRUE 1200 499
-- Not covered by a plan meeting the requirements: the Part does not apply however much they benefit.
#ASSERT NOT `reg 61 this Part applies` FALSE 1200 1200

§ `Reg 62(1) -- the reduction and the percentage`

-- 0.8% against 1.0%: the experience cost ratio is 20% less than the first payer cost ratio.
#ASSERT `reg 62(1) the percentage by which the experience cost ratio is less than the first payer cost ratio` 0.008 0.010 EQUALS JUST 0.2
#ASSERT `reg 62(1) the percentage by which the experience cost ratio is less than the first payer cost ratio` 0.0075 0.0100 EQUALS JUST 0.25
-- Equal, or greater: "is less than" is not met, so no reduction (0).
#ASSERT `reg 62(1) the percentage by which the experience cost ratio is less than the first payer cost ratio` 0.010 0.010 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `reg 62(1) the percentage by which the experience cost ratio is less than the first payer cost ratio` 0.012 0.010 EQUALS JUST 0
-- A first payer cost ratio of nothing: the percentage is undefined, so NOTHING (not covered).
#ASSERT `reg 62(1) the percentage by which the experience cost ratio is less than the first payer cost ratio` 0.008 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A rate of 2.282% reduced by 20% is 1.8256%.
#ASSERT `reg 62(1) the employer's premium rate reduced by the percentage` 0.02282 0.2 EQUALS 0.018256
#ASSERT `reg 62(1) the employer's premium rate reduced by the percentage` 0.02282 0 EQUALS 0.02282
-- Covered, plan meets the requirements, qualifying, eligibility not deferred: reduced.
#ASSERT `reg 62(1) the employer's premium rate is to be reduced in respect of the insured person` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 62(1) the employer's premium rate is to be reduced in respect of the insured person` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 62(1) the employer's premium rate is to be reduced in respect of the insured person` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 62(1) the employer's premium rate is to be reduced in respect of the insured person` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 62(1) the employer's premium rate is to be reduced in respect of the insured person` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `Reg 62(2) -- when the rate is not reduced`

-- (a) not covered; (b) covered by a plan that does not meet the requirements; (c) eligibility deferred.
#ASSERT `reg 62(2) the employer's premium rate is not to be reduced in respect of the insured person` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 62(2) the employer's premium rate is not to be reduced in respect of the insured person` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 62(2) the employer's premium rate is not to be reduced in respect of the insured person` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 62(2) the employer's premium rate is not to be reduced in respect of the insured person` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `Reg 62(3) -- the experience cost ratio`

-- For 2026 the three years ending with the second year before 2026 are 2022, 2023 and 2024.
#ASSERT `reg 62(3) the three years over which both averages are taken` 2026 EQUALS LIST 2022, 2023, 2024
-- Costs 30, 60, 90 (average 60) over earnings 6000 each (average 6000): 0.01.
#ASSERT `reg 62(3) the experience cost ratio` (LIST 30, 60, 90) (LIST 6000, 6000, 6000) EQUALS JUST 0.01
-- Not three years of each: not covered.
#ASSERT `reg 62(3) the experience cost ratio` (LIST 30, 60) (LIST 6000, 6000, 6000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 62(3) the experience cost ratio` (LIST 30, 60, 90) (LIST 6000, 6000) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Average earnings of nothing: not covered.
#ASSERT `reg 62(3) the experience cost ratio` (LIST 30, 60, 90) (LIST 0, 0, 0) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 62(4) -- the first payer cost ratio`

-- Estimated costs 200, 300, 400 (average 300) over earnings 24000 each: 300/24000 = 0.0125.
#ASSERT `reg 62(4) the first payer cost ratio` (LIST 200, 300, 400) (LIST 24000, 24000, 24000) EQUALS JUST 0.0125
#ASSERT `reg 62(4) the first payer cost ratio` (LIST 200, 300, 400, 500) (LIST 24000, 24000, 24000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 62(4) the first payer cost ratio` (LIST 200, 300, 400) (LIST 0, 0, 0) EQUALS NOTHING
